name c01m07-aces-low
timeout 2800
time 1996-03-23T19:30:00Z

# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996), CAMPAIGN ONE, SORTIE 1.7 OF 8 — "ACES LOW".
# Spec: mods/f22/doc/campaign.md 2. Geometry: mods/f22/doc/terrain.md 3. Substitutions:
# mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md. The five campaign-wide disclosures: c01m01-snake-eyes.fbm.
#
# THE TASK [TXT]: destroy the EF2000 of Flight Group `Epsilon` ON THE GROUND at Chiang Rai before they
# take off at 0315. Take-off 0230, briefed 70 NM NW; measured 71.2 NM on bearing 335.5 deg [ORF].
#
# THIS IS THE ONE SORTIE WHOSE TARGET POINT IS A REAL PLACE AND NOT A RECONSTRUCTION. Chiang Rai is
# the campaign's single anchor (terrain.md 2.1): the game names it, and FOB Tyler's coordinate is
# DERIVED FROM IT, not the other way round. The target here is therefore 19.90868 N / 99.82791 E, the
# city centroid — and terrain.md 5.3 records that the real Chiang Rai International (VTCT) is 7.5 km
# NE of it. The airfield is NOT snapped to VTCT: re-anchoring is a decision terrain.md leaves open and
# taking it here would move all eight sorties.
#
# SUBSTITUTIONS IN THIS FILE
#   EF2000 PARKED ON THE RAMP -> `target_soft` x 2, 150 m apart. FlightBox has NO aircraft-on-the-
#     ground-that-later-takes-off: a `module` with an FDM spawned at zero speed is an aeroplane sitting
#     still, not a scheduled departure, and there is no way to declare "this unit starts rolling at
#     t = X". A parked airframe is an unarmoured object, which is what the soft fragility class
#     describes. WHAT IS THEREBY NOT MEASURED: they cannot escape, so the sortie cannot fail the way
#     the original could.
#   EF2000 AIRBORNE CAP -> `f15c` (F-15C). The catalogue has no Eurofighter. `f15c` is its only T4
#     PEER row that is not Soviet: twin-engine, 8 stations, a gun, and a measured roll plant so it can
#     fight. The error, named: no supercruise, no canard-delta, no helmet sight; a 160 km APG-63
#     against a Captor whose reach nothing in the sources gives. It is a peer-class western fighter
#     standing in for a peer-class western fighter, which is the closest this catalogue gets.
#   `RDAR_03` -> `p18`. An early-warning antenna with no weapon: it finds and it radiates, and that is
#     all the .ORF's model name claims.
#   SA-2 -> `sa2`. EXACT.
#   GBU-30 JDAM -> `mk84`, the campaign-wide rule (c01m03-luckiest-man-in-laos.fbm).
#
# "BEFORE THEY TAKE OFF" IS A DECLARED SPAN, AND IT DOES NOT BIND ON THIS INGRESS — SAID PLAINLY.
# 0230 to 0315 is 45 min = 2 700 s, and `objective kill unit s7ef1 until 2700` freezes the objective's
# state at that instant (doc/missions/verdict.md). The ingress is 60 km at 450 kt = 260 s, so the
# deadline has ~2 440 s of slack and no run that flies this route can miss it. IT IS DECLARED ANYWAY,
# for two reasons: it is the mission's actual condition and belongs in the file rather than in a
# comment asking a reader to check a timestamp; and it fails a run that is DIVERTED, which is the only
# way this sortie can lose the race with the engine as it stands.
#
# NIGHT. 0230 local at the equinox is deep night (disclosure D4). The `mission CLOCK` line at t = 0
# gives the computed sun elevation at the primary actor's spawn and is the check. What that buys and
# what it does not: the visual channel of `sensors/FBVisualSystem` reads ZERO at night, so the ZU-23
# class of gun would see nothing here — which is why this sortie's ground defence is a RADAR SAM and
# a radar, not a gun. Nothing about the renderer is exercised by `fb-gym`.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `s7lead`'s and `s7two`'s UNIT_RESULT, read together.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 = both EF2000 objects destroyed INSIDE the declared window and both strikers alive.
#   One aircraft destroyed is a MISSION LOSS and reads as TIMEOUT/exit 3 with the unmet `kill` named.
#   A `kill` that is `state=unmet` while the object's own UNIT_RESULT reads DESTROYED would mean the
#   kill landed after t = 2 700 — an ENGINE finding about the window, not a mission result. Check the
#   `damage KILL` timestamp before reporting either way.
#   Dying to the SA-2 or to the F-15C is a mission loss (exit 1), not a defect.
#   THE THING THIS FILE CANNOT SAY, and campaign.md asks for it explicitly: whether a kill happened
#   before or after ROTATION. Nothing rotates. The two cases the original distinguishes collapse into
#   one here, and no reading of this file's output separates them.

# MEASURED (exit 3, real ground): THE SA-2 BELT NO LONGER GETS THE STRIKE, AND ONE EF2000 BURNS.
#   t = 0.0 s           `mission CLOCK sunElDeg=-53.181` — deep night, which is the check on D4's date
#   t = 133.7-177.0 s   six v-750 in two salvoes at the SAME six timestamps as over the flat plane;
#                       launch ranges 22 907 / 22 099 / 21 407 / 14 283 / 13 598 / 12 914 m against
#                       22 955 / 22 149 / 21 459 / 14 360 / 13 679 / 13 000 m over the plane — 48-86 m
#                       shorter, because the battery now stands on 395 m of ground
#   t = 202.4 s         round FIVE detonates 11.80 m from `s7lead` AND DOES NOT KILL IT. Over the flat
#                       plane it was round FOUR at 8.20 m, and that one did
#   t = 209-213 s       rounds 1,2,3,4,6 fly on past the target and CFIT into the 403-431 m valley
#                       floor 8-11 km SOUTH of the belt
#   t = 260.0 s         `s7two` puts its mk84 on `s7ef2`: DESTROYED
#   verdict             `s7two` SUCCESS, `s7lead` TIMEOUT (`s7ef1` INTACT), `s7esc` TIMEOUT, exit 3
#
# THE HEADLINE, AND ITS MARGIN, BOTH STATED. "The SA-2 kills the attack 12.1 km before the ramp" was a
# FLAT-PLANE result and does not survive real ground: same battery, same six rounds, same seconds, no
# kill. The CAUSE is that the launcher sits 395 m higher, so every intercept geometry shifts. The
# MARGIN is 3.6 m of miss distance (8.20 -> 11.80), i.e. the flat-plane kill was already inside the
# noise of its own geometry. Do not read this as "the SA-2 is harmless"; read it as "the flat plane
# was deciding this sortie, and it was deciding it on a knife edge."
# The F-15C 150 km out still never entered the fight.

unit s7lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm7 1
  spawn 19.41822 100.06526 3000 335.5 450     # 60 km down-track of Chiang Rai, above the SA-2's floor
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 19.90868 99.82791 3000 450               # ITS aim point: the first parked Eurofighter
  wp 20.07217 99.74863 3000 450               # egress 20 km beyond the field
  objective kill unit s7ef1 until 2700
  objective survive

unit s7two
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm7 2
  spawn 19.42381 100.07827 3000 335.5 450     # 1.5 km across track from the leader
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 19.90868 99.82934 3000 450               # ITS aim point: the second, 150 m east
  wp 20.07217 99.74863 3000 450
  objective kill unit s7ef2 until 2700
  objective survive

unit s7esc
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm7 3
  spawn 19.41000 100.08500 5000 335.5 480     # high cover, behind and above the pair
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 21.13482 99.23126 5000 480               # toward the CAP
  objective kill unit s7cap
  objective protect unit s7lead
  objective survive

unit s7cap
  module f15c
  team hostile
  spawn 21.13482 99.23126 6000 155.5 480      # 150 km beyond the field: the merge is AFTER the strike
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 155 150 5000
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 19.41822 100.06526 6000 480
  objective survive

unit s7ef1
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 19.90868 99.82791 ground 335.5 0      # Flight Group Epsilon, parked

unit s7ef2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 19.90868 99.82934 ground 335.5 0      # 150 m east

unit s7sam
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 19.85963 99.85168 ground 335.5 0      # 6 km short of the field, ON the run-in
  set alert ready
  set emcon free

unit s7rdr
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 19.94138 99.81206 ground 335.5 0      # 4 km beyond the field
  set emcon free
